  "lineage": "Communal song-and-dance repertoire of the Ainu of Hokkaido and formerly Sakhalin, performed seated in a circle around a lidded shintoko container beaten as a drum for upopo round-songs sung in short overlapping canon, and standing for rimse circle dances such as the crane dance sarorun rimse and the sword dance emush rimse, with tonkori zither and mukkuri bamboo jaw harp providing instrumental colour; documented in Pilsudski's 1902-1905 cylinders and revived from the 1960s through preservation societies at Shiraoi and Akan.",
